# Cursor rules
#
# The canonical rules for every AI agent live in AGENTS.md. Read it before acting.
# Summary of the non-negotiable rules (AGENTS.md wins on any conflict):

- Read AGENTS.md, docs/project-context/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md and .harness/state/session-handoff.md at the start of every session.
- If asked to create a new project from this template, follow BOOTSTRAP.md exactly.
- Do ONLY what the user asked. No unrequested refactors, features, dependencies or reformatting.
- ALWAYS ask before doing anything that was not explicitly requested. Propose, then wait for a yes.
- Ask clarifying questions when requirements are ambiguous or incomplete, before writing code.
- Run lint, format check, type check and tests (commands in .harness/env/sandbox.config) before every commit. Never use --no-verify.
- Never commit secrets or .env files.
- Never push to main, force-push or rewrite history unless explicitly asked for that exact action.
- Confirm before destructive or outward-facing actions (delete, deploy, migrate, create/close issues).
- One GitHub issue at a time. Check docs/process/definition-of-ready.md before starting and docs/process/definition-of-done.md + .harness/templates/clean-state-checklist.md before calling it done.
- Never fabricate test results. Report failures with real output.
- At the end of a session, update .harness/state/claude-progress.md and .harness/state/session-handoff.md.
